    Key Takeaways & Lessons Learned include the following questions:

        What did the successful case do right?
            • Engaged employees early and provided training.
            • Partnered with experts to tailor ERP solutions.
            • Ensured realistic goals and gradual implementation.

        What went wrong in the failed case?
            • Rushed implementation with unrealistic expectations.
            • Insufficient testing before going live.
            • Lack of change management and employee involvement.

        How can future implementations avoid similar failures?
            • Define clear business requirements and test rigorously before deployment.
            • Engage employees and train them on new systems.
            • Implement in phases rather than an all-at-once approach.


Insights & recommendations

    Best Practices for Successful Enterprise System Implementation:
        • Conduct thorough business process analysis before selecting an ERP.
        • Engage key stakeholders and ensure employee buy-in.
        • Perform rigorous testing before full deployment.
        • Choose a phased implementation strategy to minimize risks.

    Strategies to Avoid Failure:
        • Set realistic implementation goals.
        • Align ERP functionality with business needs.
        • Allocate sufficient time for system testing.
        • Ensure a structured change management process.

